  "title": "PCYT2 and SELENOI perturbations activate a TH Prkcd/Grin2c SREBP cholesterol program and reveal a peptide-processing branch downstream of PCYT2",
  "status": "grounded",
  "rejection_reason": null,
  "exact_observed_result": "Pcyt2 perturbation in 151 TH induced sterol genes including Insig1, Cyp51, Msmo1, Fdft1, Ldlr, Hmgcr, Hmgcs1, and Srebf2 at FDR<0.05, and reduced Cpe and Pcsk2 in the same cells. Selenoi was directly depleted in 151 TH and induced the overlapping Insig1/Msmo1/Fdft1/Hmgcr sterol arm.",
  "biological_interpretation": "Two CDP-ethanolamine phosphatidylethanolamine-pathway perturbations converge on a thalamic SREBP-like transcriptional compensation state, while PCYT2 additionally depresses secretory peptide-processing transcripts.",
